  "conditions": "RTX 3050. 6-second Orda renderer samples after warmup, 22 animated monsters and 5 participants, fixed 1669x939 framebuffer in 1920x1080 window. Before: 5 cameras. After: 1, 3, 5 human cameras. No full AI/network/game simulation in benchmark. Native solo application rendering still uses scaling 1; fixed 1.15 is benchmark-only to compare equal pixel budgets.",
  "changes": [
    "Human-only view ownership shared by Orda, Backrooms, Sparatoria, Ribaltati; bots remain in simulation, avatars and results.",
    "Solo owns a full-screen viewport. Friends using phone or pad own their own viewport.",
    "Backrooms cameras, masks, jumpscares, spectator selection and stereo pan mapped to human identities, without creating bot-only UI/scare actors.",
    "Orda no longer creates bot viewmodels/HUD/cameras; the solo first-person avatar is not instantiated when invisible to every camera.",
    "Cached split layouts and unused pointer picking disabled; original graphics preserved.",
    "Shared-camera and turn-based games retain their single world camera."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Short renderer benchmark, not a guarantee of multiplayer session FPS.",
